 61ZN    40CA(24MG,2PNG):T:XUNDL-8     2017QU05                           201710
 61ZN c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2017Qu05:                          
 61ZN2c  Phys. Rev. C 96, 044313 (2017)                                         
 61ZN c  Includes {+58}Ni(|a,n) reaction                                        
 61ZN c  Compiled by C.D. Nesaraja (ORNL)                                       
 61ZN c  20 October, 2017                                                       
 61ZN c  A recoil-distance Doppler-shift (RDDS) experiment                      
 61ZN2c  was performed at the FN-Tandem accelerator at the Institute for        
 61ZN3c  Nuclear Physics, University of Cologne to measure lifetimes of excited 
 61ZN4c  states in {+61}Zn using two different reactions.                       
 61ZN c  {+40}Ca({+24}Mg, 2pn|g): E({+24}Mg)= 77 MeV (energy was listed as      
 61ZN2c  67 MeV in the abstract) impinged a {+40}Ca target that was evaporated  
 61ZN3c  on gold backing. {+61}Zn recoils were stopped in a separate thick      
 61ZN4c  tantalum foil. Utilizing the Cologne plunger device, seven             
 61ZN5c  target-to-stopper distances were chosen in the range from 41.7 to      
 61ZN6c  140.6 |mm. An array of twelve HPGe detectors was used to detect        
 61ZN7c  the emitted |g rays. The detectors placed in rings at 0|' (1 detector),
 61ZN8c  45|'(6 detectors), and 143|' (5 detectors) with respect to the beam    
 61ZN9c  axis. Background radiation arising from X-rays was reduced by          
 61ZNac  shielding each detector with 2-mm-thick sheets of lead and copper.     
 61ZNbc  The analysis was performed by employing the differential decay curve   
 61ZNcc  method (DDCM) in coincidence mode which eliminated any                 
 61ZNdc  uncertainties imposed by unknown side feeding                          
 61ZN c  {+58}Ni(|a, n): E(|a)= 19 MeV impinged a {+58}Ni target.               
 61ZN2c  {+61}Zn recoils were stopped in the self-supporting target.            
 61ZN3c  A detector array consisting of 8 HPGe and 8 cerium-doped               
 61ZN4c  lanthanum bromide (LaBr3:Ce) detectors, mounted in the                 
 61ZN5c  frame of the HORUS array was used for |g ray detection. Six of the     
 61ZN6c  LaBr3:Ce detectors were surrounded by BGO veto detectors to suppress   
 61ZN7c  the Compton background. Copper sheets were used to reduce background   
 61ZN8c  from X-rays. Data were sorted into six correlation group matrices,     
 61ZN9c  each associated with detector pairs at angles |q{-1,2} with respect    
 61ZNbc  to the beam axis and a relative angle |F between the planes spanned    
 61ZNcc  by the detectors and the beam axis.                                    
 61ZN c  Measured: E|g, |g|g-coin, lifetime with the recoil-distance Doppler-   
 61ZN2c  shift (RDDS) method (|t in the order of picoseconds) and the           
 61ZN3c  electronic fast timing method (|t in the nanosecond region)            
 61ZN c  Deduced: Mixing ratios and reduced transition strengths                
 61ZN c  Theoretical Analysis: Comparison of measured lifetimes and level       
 61ZN2c  energies with shell model calculations (NUSHELLX@MSU) in the fp,       
 61ZN3c  f{-5/2}pg{-9/2}, and multishell fp-g{-9/2}d{-5/2} model spaces.        
 61ZN c  Level scheme is from 2006An31: Eur.Phys.J. A 30, 381 (2006)            
 61ZN2c  Energies were rounded off to the nearest keV.                          
